# Plex Media Server is now supported in the Streaming Dashboard

### What's new

**Plex Media Server is now a first-class streaming backend in QuickBox Pro**, alongside the existing Emby and Jellyfin integrations. The What's Streaming Dashboard (WSDashboard) auto-detects a Plex install, auto-populates the server URL and token after install, and treats Plex sessions on full parity with the other two media servers - sessions, watch analytics, history, top items, intents, libraries, the per-item detail page, and the admin Playback Mirror all work against Plex out of the box.

This is the single biggest streaming-side expansion since WSDashboard launched.

### Other improvements in this release

- **Rate / vote from item cards.** Mark a five-star rating or heart-toggle a favorite directly from the streaming item card on Emby, Jellyfin, and Plex.
- **Mark watched / unwatched** from item cards on Emby and Jellyfin.
- **Responsiveness pass.** Denser layouts, better mobile and tablet behavior, and glassmorphic consistency across the System Dashboard widgets.
- **History and Analytics polish.** Better contrast on the Watch History title cells, Live TV channel logos render at the correct fit, episode rows now display the show poster instead of per-episode screenshots, and admins can pin which media types appear in their Top Watched panel - saved per user.
- **Playback Mirror parity.** The admin floating mirror dock now works against all three media servers and pre-rolls the upstream transcoder so the mirror opens in sync with the source user's stream instead of trailing behind.

### How to get it

Run `qb update quickbox` once the next public release is available, or wait for the dashboard auto-update to pick it up.

If you have not installed Plex yet, the canonical install passes the target user (and optionally a [plex.tv claim token](https://plex.tv/claim) for one-step server claim):

```bash
qb install plex -u username -pct 'claim-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx'
```

The `-u` flag is required. The `-pct` token is optional but recommended - when present, the CLI reads it from Plex's own `Preferences.xml` after install and writes the resulting `X-Plex-Token` into the dashboard automatically. No settings-page round trip. The full set of install flags (`-u`, `-pct`, `-D` for a custom data directory, `-d` for a reverse-proxy domain) is documented at `https://v3.quickbox.io/docs/applications/media-servers/plex`.

